# 🔄 HOW IT WORKS

```text id="f1"
Laptop (Browser/App)
        ↓
SOCKS Proxy (127.0.0.1:1080)
        ↓
SSH Tunnel (encrypted)
        ↓
Remote Server
        ↓
Internet / Internal Network
```

---

# 🔐 SECURITY LEVEL

✔ Encrypted (SSH tunnel)
✔ No open internet ports
✔ Safer on public networks

⚠ But:

* depends on trusted SSH server
* not full VPN replacement
* only proxy-aware apps use it

---

# 🧠 SIMPLE DIFFERENCE

| Type | Purpose                    |
| ---- | -------------------------- |
| `-L` | One service forwarding     |
| `-R` | Publish local service      |
| `-D` | Full traffic proxy (SOCKS) |

---

# 🏁 FINAL SUMMARY

```text id="final"
Dynamic Port Forwarding (-D) creates a SOCKS proxy that routes all application traffic through a secure SSH tunnel to a remote server.
```

